  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday) \nIssued at 1130 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nSurface ridging will gradually slide eastward from the latter half\nof the week into the weekend while modest mid level ridging builds\nback eastward and flattens out of the southern states. All in all,\nthis will lead to near persistent conditions across the forecast\narea through the late half of the workweek and through the\nweekend. Dry conditions, with clear skies and generally light\nsoutheast to southerly winds expected to continue. The dry\nconditions will continue to favor near normal, cool overnight lows\nin the 50s, warming into the mid to upper 80s for most places by\nthe afternoon. \n\nA tropical wave will lift north out of the Gulf through the\nweekend, but guidance continues to indicate this system will stay\nto the east of the forecast area, with little to no impact for us.\nA few showers could affect portions of western Arkansas Saturday\nnight into Sunday, but chances and amounts remain low for now.\nWinds look to pick up during the back half of the forecast, which\ncould again raise fire weather concerns as drought continues its\nhold on much of the forecast area. A stronger storm system and\nassociated cold front could bring increasing rain chances toward \nthe middle part of next week, but that remains outside of the \nforecast package at this time.\n\nBowlan",
